      "title": "Russia considers changing funding rules for adults with rare diseases",
      "content_html": "Russia’s Health Ministry acknowledged that federal co-funding rules for orphan medicines need revision after a roundtable heard that adults can lose access to treatment when they age out of the children’s charity Circle of Kindness and responsibility shifts to regional governments. The reserve funding mechanism, introduced this year for regions in need, has eligibility criteria that some regions say bar them from support despite rising costs.\n\nA review of data from 81 regions found that only 14 reported sufficient funding, while 63 reported lawsuits by patients seeking free medicines. Of 74 rulings in patients’ favor, 34% were implemented within one to two months, 53% took three to six months, and 13% took a year or more. Deputy Health Minister Sergei Glagolev said the ministry should examine how the rules work in practice and improve the criteria.",
